88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (The Simple Inventory Tracker is a console-based application developed using Java. It is designed to manage basic product information, including Product ID, product name, quantity, and price. The application allows users to add new products, view all available products, search for products using their Product ID, and sort products according to their name and price.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (The project uses the Java Collections Framework, particularly ArrayList, to store product details dynamically. Searching is implemented using a linear search technique, while sorting is performed using Java's Collections.sort\(\) method and Comparator. The application also demonstrates Object-Oriented Programming concepts through classes, objects, constructors, and methods. Scanner is used to accept user input, and a menu-driven interface makes the application simple to operate.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (The main objective of this project is to understand the practical implementation of data structures and algorithms in Java. It provides a basic approach to inventory management without requiring a database or complex technologies. All product information is stored temporarily in memory during program execution. The project can be further enhanced by adding file handling, database connectivity, product updates, deletion, and low-stock alerts.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (Overall, the Simple Inventory Tracker demonstrates how Java programming, ArrayList, searching, and sorting can be combined to develop a simple and useful inventory management application.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
